<TEXT>&#2;
<TITLE>BAHIA COCOA REVIEW</TITLE>
<DATELINE>    SALVADOR, Feb 26 - </DATELINE><BODY>Showers continued throughout the week in the Bahia cocoa zone, alleviating the drought since early January and improving prospects for the coming temporao, although normal humidity levels have not yet been restored.
    Comissaria Smith said in its weekly review that 430,000 bags of 60 kilos each had been purchased by shippers so far for 1987/88 temporao.
    Reflecting the improved crop prospects, prices fell to between 345 and 350 cruzados per arroba.
    Total Bahia sales for 1986/87 were estimated at 6.13 mln bags.
 Reuter
&#3;</BODY></TEXT>
</REUTERS>
