<PLACES><D>usa</D></PLACES>
<TEXT>&#2;
<TITLE>TALKING POINT/BANKAMERICA EQUITY OFFERING</TITLE>
<DATELINE>    SAN FRANCISCO, Feb 26 - </DATELINE><BODY>BankAmerica Corp is expected to complete its proposed 1.0 billion dlr capital restructuring by mid-year, analysts said.
    The plan includes issuing 400 mln dlrs of preferred stock and 350 mln dlrs of convertible debt.
    Analysts believe the common stock market will respond favorably if commercial banking margins improve.
    BankAmerica has faced severe pressure from First Interstate Bancorp takeover bids.
 Reuter
&#3;</BODY></TEXT>
</REUTERS>
<REUTERS TOPICS="YES" LEWISSPLIT="TRAIN" CGISPLIT="TRAINING-SET" OLDID="5548" NEWID="5">
<DATE>26-FEB-1987 15:10:44.60</DATE>
<TOPICS><D>earn</D></TOPICS>
<PLACES><D>usa</D></PLACES>
<TEXT>&#2;
<TITLE>COMPUTER TERMINAL SYSTEMS COMPLETES RESTRUCTURING</TITLE>
<DATELINE>    COMMACK, N.Y., Feb 26 - </DATELINE><BODY>Computer Terminal Systems Inc said it completed the sale of 200,000 shares of common stock for 1.2 mln dlrs.
    The proceeds will be used to pay off existing creditors and for working capital to support new printer manufacturing operations.
    The company said management expects positive operating cash flow by the third quarter of 1987.
 Reuter
&#3;</BODY></TEXT>
</REUTERS>
